  Crebbp:
    'Crebbp, the mouse form of CREBBP, informs models built around cancer relevant pathway activity spanning driver signaling, repair, or tumor microenvironment. The modeling decision is less about novelty and more about matching mutation timing to patient somatic events. If embryonic lethality blocks colony expansion, do not force a homozygous null for an adult oncology endpoint; move to conditional or mosaic strategies. Patient variant knockins move beyond null alleles into genotype aligned pharmacology and resistance studies that better match clinical CREBBP mutations. Define success as latent tumor control, metastasis metrics, or drug response before locking the Crebbp allele plan. Crossing Crebbp alleles to Kras, Trp53, or Myc backgrounds remains a standard way to test cooperation, latency, and therapy response.',
  Cstb:
    'Cstb is widely requested because it supports immune pathway activity that shapes host defense, tolerance, or inflammatory disease. Global deletion can be informative, yet cell restricted conditional alleles usually give cleaner mechanism readouts. Epitope matched humanization at Cstb also helps when diagnostic reagents and clinical candidates share human selective binding surfaces. Conditional deletion in T cells, B cells, myeloid cells, or epithelium assigns which compartment actually drives the phenotype when Cstb is broadly expressed. For translational immuno oncology, humanized targets plus syngeneic or humanized immune contexts usually outperform mouse only nulls at this locus. If your primary assay is antibody blockade of CSTB, plan humanized Cstb early and use mouse nulls mainly to prove pathway necessity.',
  Ctla4:
    'Immune model design for Ctla4 centers on immune pathway activity that shapes host defense, tolerance, or inflammatory disease. Human CTLA4 aligned questions then push the plan toward humanized targets when antibodies are the product. If your primary assay is antibody blockade of CTLA4, plan humanized Ctla4 early and use mouse nulls mainly to prove pathway necessity. Global knockout can unleash systemic inflammation or immunodeficiency, so tissue restricted or cell type specific conditional alleles often yield cleaner mechanism readouts for Ctla4. Align Cre driver choice with the immune compartment named in your primary endpoint before locking production alleles. Knockin alleles that preserve expression under native regulation beat random transgenic overexpression for dosage sensitive cytokines and receptors such as Ctla4.',
