    'Cancer genetics programs treat Kdm6a as a handle on cancer relevant pathway activity spanning driver signaling, repair, or tumor microenvironment; also referenced as UTX in some literature. Tissue restricted and inducible designs usually beat constitutive alleles for adult tumor windows. Define success as latent tumor control, metastasis metrics, or drug response before locking the Kdm6a allele plan. Tissue restricted and inducible alleles let tumors arise after development, which better mirrors somatic mutation timing in patients carrying KDM6A pathway lesions. Humanized immune checkpoint partners are often combined when the readout is immunotherapy rather than tumor genetics alone at Kdm6a. Activating knockins and floxed stop cassettes are preferred for oncogenes where simple deletion of Kdm6a answers the wrong biological question.',
  Kit:
    'Oncology demand for Kit stays high because cancer relevant pathway activity spanning driver signaling, repair, or tumor microenvironment sits on common therapy and resistance paths that need genetically defined mouse cohorts. Conventional knockout is useful for tumor suppressor dosage studies when homozygous loss of Kit is tolerated long enough to score cancer endpoints. Define success as latent tumor control, metastasis metrics, or drug response before locking the Kit allele plan. Humanized Kit supports antibody, ADC, and degrader programs that require human KIT extracellular or epitope sequence inside a murine host. Match allele class to genetics: null or floxed for suppressors, activating knockin for drivers, humanized for biologics aimed at KIT.',
